 ## Overview
-The Two-pass Spectral Rendering Integral is a method for computing volumetric shadows in participating media by adapting the Kajiya and von Herzen two-pass algorithm to spectral representation [S1, book]. It separates shadow computation (illumination phase) from radiance accumulation (radiation phase), allowing for the simulation of complex spectral effects such as fluorescence and phosphorescence [S1, book]. It is distinguished from its parent [Two-Pass Shadow Casting (Kajiya and Von Herzen)](2196-two-pass-shadow-casting-kajiya-and-von-herzen.md) by its explicit handling of wavelength-dependent opacity and emission spectra.
